# editor / agent scratch
# "When NYC Government Goes Open Source by Default" — a draft roadmap that is
# NOT for this public repo. It is expected to become an independent document and
# site on wegovnyc later. Untracked 2026-08-07; the file stays on disk at
# docs/OPEN-SOURCE-BY-DEFAULT.md so work can continue on it locally.
#
# ⚠ This only stops FUTURE commits. The draft was pushed publicly in four
# commits (8462c02, 6f3e02e, 5f7b029, ab1b6f7) and remains readable in this
# repo's history on GitHub until those are purged. Do not re-add it.
docs/OPEN-SOURCE-BY-DEFAULT.md

# `.claude/*`, NOT `.claude/` — git cannot re-include a file whose parent
# DIRECTORY is excluded, so the negation below is silently ignored with the
# trailing-slash form. Ignoring the contents instead makes it work.
.claude/*
# Shared project settings are tracked: they carry the PreToolUse hook that
# refuses blanket `git add -A` here, and it has to reach the other sessions and
# clones it exists to protect. launch.json and settings.local.json stay local.
!.claude/settings.json
